  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "While inspecting the sovereign immortal fetus Gu body and its new rank six blessed land, Fang Yuan contrasts ordinary high, medium, and low grade starting lands with the ten extreme physiques. He lists Great Strength True Martial Physique, Northern Dark Ice Soul Physique, Verdant Great Sun Physique, and Desolate Ancient Moon Physique among that set. Once a person of the ten extreme physiques becomes a Gu Immortal, as with Hei Lou Lan, they obtain a super grade blessed land whose starting territory is over 6700 km2 and does not exceed 13000 km2.",
      "chapters": [
        1027
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_sovereign_immortal_fetus_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_great_strength_true_martial_physique",
        "sys_northern_dark_ice_soul_physique",
        "sys_desolate_ancient_moon_physique",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Broader set rules sit on Ten Extreme Physique.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_ten_extreme_physique"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No chapter names a living holder of this physique; the corpus places the name only on Ren Zu’s eldest son, Verdant Great Sun, in myth.",
      "chapters": [
        135
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ren_zu",
        "char_verdant_great_sun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Legends of Ren Zu records that cognition Gu gave Verdant Great Sun a pair of wings, which he used to fly higher and higher while chasing glory, until the wings burst and his fall killed him.",
      "chapters": [
        371
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ren-zus-eldest-son",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
        "gu_cognition_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hairy men of the immemorial era once tied him up, attempting to use him to refine an eternal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        486
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ren-zus-eldest-son",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_eternal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the present-day story, Fang Yuan’s intel places Verdant Great Sun’s soul inside the Door of Life and Death alongside Spectral Soul Demon Venerable’s main body.",
      "chapters": [
        2192
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "held-inside-the-door-of-life-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_door_of_life_and_death",
        "char_spectral_soul_demon_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When a figure disrupts Paradise Earth’s killer move there, Fang Yuan suspects Verdant Great Sun: his soul had lain at Pacifying Soul Lake, and it appears Spectral Soul Demon Venerable, unable to fully consume it, is instead being controlled by it.",
      "chapters": [
        2197
      ],
